# quality-mgr, 2026-09-05, qa-pr1220-r1: closing this record for the
# approved ruling scope (peer write envelope version + major-reject/minor-
# tolerate + 1.1.0 baseline), confirmed on fix/av-hotfix-crosshost @
# 295ae10d4. crates/atm-core/src/protocol.rs:96 HTTP_API_VERSION = "1.1.0".
# crates/atm-core/src/send/mod.rs -- WriteRequest.peer_http_api_version +
# with_peer_http_api_version(). crates/atm-http-runtime/src/message_handler.rs:228-240
# validate_peer_write_version compares only .major(); missing version
# defaults to current (backward compatible); rejects only major mismatch,
# naming both versions, via AtmErrorCode::ClientDaemonVersionIncompatible.
# Test peer_write_version_tolerates_minor_skew_and_rejects_major_skew
# confirmed present. Wiring the still-dead CLI preflight
# (verify_connection_compatibility), doctor version reporting, and an
# envelope-change guard test were explicitly NOT part of this ruling's
# approved scope -- left open, not part of this closure.
# Open follow-up (Important, non-blocking, new finding not part of this
# closure): docs/atm-daemon/http-api.md and docs/atm-http-runtime/openapi.yaml
# were not updated to reflect the 1.1.0 bump or the new peer_http_api_version
# field, per ADR-061 D3's same-change-set documentation requirement.

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AV-HOTFIX-003/AV4-fixed-295ae10d4>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "crates/atm-core/src/protocol.rs" ;
  triage:line 96 ;
  triage:snippet "HTTP_API_VERSION = \"1.1.0\"; validate_peer_write_version rejects only a major mismatch, naming both versions" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
